title The tier for what a host can do -- the roster's third field, and the control that plants absence without an override
prompt Kyri seat prompt for SILENCE: read KYRI and GAUGE_STYLE, honor the ITINERARY INNER LOOP standing block, walk the newest day shelf for the running thread, take the infrastructure-Glow lane, open with ListAgents and name any peer before a file moves, send the twice-pulled way, stop at the custody gates.
think Rota row: N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3750, so 3750 mod 5 = 0 -- AETHER, the row that hears, and not a repeat of the previous lap's water (N=3748, row 3), so no hand-advance. Read the threshold plus all three: follow-our-compass (the return habit, brief and green witnesses beating the plan), the Lindy effect (a plain word read on the first day still reads on the ten-thousandth), and the grain and the crossing (ten strands; a guard that cannot red guards nothing). The sentence the row hands forward: the work exists so a promise the tree makes can be checked by whoever runs it, which is why an unrunnable guard and an unprovable claim cost the same thing.
think ListAgents at the open named one peer, grain-65. Mid-lap the harness reported construction/standing-equipment.kyri modified; git status read it STAGED, not mine -- the peer seating wire_lab_fn_drift, exactly their own 15:31:50 recommend line. That is REDS %291 alive on the bench rather than in the ledger, so I sent them the file name, the split I was taking, and the path-limited-commit promise before anything of mine moved. They landed 908f99fac7 during the lap; my seven files were unstaged and survived it.
think Reds first. The cold roster read 93 guards, 86 green, 7 red, tree_moved=yes (the peer's staging moved the digest between open and close, which is the honest reading rather than a fault of mine). Four reds beyond the card's three: two Pond rows already named as Hush's door, nib_honesty and remember_git_nib both closing on this send's nib refresh, and reds_status_consistency, whose own CONTROL held two red cases.
think The reds_status_consistency root, found by git log -S rather than by reading the scan: commit 344e349b2 ("reds: BOOKED, the third status word") changed fold_blocked_rows to count only MARKERLESS rows carrying the bare word OPEN, and did not touch the control. The control still planted a MARKED row and expected a hit, so fold_blocked_counted and fold_blocked_named had stood RED from door B and the whole guard was off. That is docs-implementation-sync one layer over: a control is a guard's proof, and a stale proof turns the guard off rather than merely dating it.
think The keystone is the roster's own booked design question, written in construction/standing-equipment.kyri lines 594-601: comlink_r1_dual_stack stands off the roster because its leg B reds on a host without IPv6, and the note says plainly that `host macos` cannot carry it -- host is a tier for PLACE and this condition is one of CAPABILITY, so the OS word would encode something untrue. The note declined to guess and named the question on the card. This lap makes the guess and proves it.
think The mechanism is the exact sibling of `host` (REDS %295): a `capability` field, refused by the scan when it names a word no runner probes, counted as guards_capability_gated and guards_unknown_capability, and in the runner a probe returning THREE answers rather than two. Present runs. Absent is skipped by name -- `skipped_capability needs_six wants=ipv6 here=absent` -- and counted. Unknown RUNS the guard, and that third answer is the whole safety of the field: skipping on an unknown is how a capability tier stops being a cadence and becomes an exemption, thinning a roster to nothing on some future bench whose probe tools went missing while every meter reads green. The runner probes only the words the roster actually asks for, so no second copy of the scan's list exists to drift against it.
think Planting absence without putting an override into the runner was the crux of the control. The probe reads the host through `ip` and `ifconfig`, so the control shadows those two on PATH and hands it a fake host: a stub printing `inet6 ::1` for present, one printing only 127.0.0.1 for absent, one exiting 1 for unknown. Nothing in the runner learns it is being tested and there is no environment variable that turns the field off -- a gate with a door beside it is a habit again, and the control would have been the one holding the door. The first draft of that helper passed the stub's own body to the runner as a guard name (no shift), which read as a one-guard pass and made all six capability cases answer no; the shift is now commented as load-bearing.
obs Found while seating the new field beside it: `host` arrived at REDS %295 with NO case in the control and NO assertion in the witness, so the axis this one copies had neither a green side nor a red one. Three host cases and four assertions are seated now, against the host the pass actually stands on. Copying an unproven pattern would have doubled it.
obs The honest limit of the capability tier, said rather than smoothed: for comlink_r1_dual_stack the probe and leg B read the SAME interface table, so once the tier holds the ::1 question, leg B's ::1 assertion can no longer red for a tree reason. That is the %311 family -- checker and checked sharing a source -- and the right reading is that the tier takes the ENVIRONMENT half while leg A, which lowers and runs the tree's own pedestal, policy face and width face, keeps every tooth it had. Engineering a fake independence would have been worse than naming this.
obs Three recited counts shed on touch, all the same drift: the reds control header said twenty-nine while running thirty-four, its witness green line said "control 32/32", and the standing-equipment witness said "forty-three behaviors" in its header and "sixty-two behaviors" in its closing line while the control ran eighty-five. A recited total is the one part of a green line that goes false while every assertion above it still holds. Each now names the reading instead of the number, and the controls print their own tallies.
obs Booked no REDS row for any of it, and the reason is a standing gate rather than a judgment: the pin reads 24,476 of 24,576 bytes with 100 free, 8 OPEN and 0 foldable, so pin_deadlocked=1 stands and a new row cannot fit. The reds_status_consistency repair closes on a witness on metal; the leg B header claim is repaired in place under docs-implementation-sync.
obs The roster's own witness reds against the live run card whenever that card holds any red, which is REDS %328's open seat exactly ("whether the roster's own witness can be rostered at all"). Proven green here against a red-free card, so the new assertions are known to pass and the live red is the documented deadlock rather than a regression.
